{"uid":"modules/ttpscope_bridge.py","name":"ttpscope_bridge.py","qualname":"modules/ttpscope_bridge.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/ttpscope_bridge.py","line":1,"end_line":713,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Secure bridge for the TTPScope MITRE ATT&CK research client.","description":"Wraps the ``ttpscope`` C binary (built from\nhttps://github.com/bl4ckr0ss3/ttpscope) so CLI operators, MCP agents,\nand the autonomous loop share one validated, non-interactive path.\n\nSecurity invariants:\n    1. No shell execution — argv list-form via safe_run_argv only.\n    2. Technique/object IDs validated before reaching the binary.\n    3. Free-text queries length-capped and passed as single argv element.\n    4. Output truncated (200 KB) and always staged under sessions/.\n    5. ``chain`` action joins ttpscope + atomic_resolver + parquet\n       without executing anything on a target.\n\nFallback independence (no hard dependency on ttpscope):\n    When the binary is missing or unusable, every read action degrades\n    to an embedded backend: the cached STIX bundle\n    (``~/.cache/ttpscope/enterprise-attack.json``, synced via stdlib\n    urllib) is queried directly, and ``parquets/techniques*.parquet``\n    covers Atomic technique lookups. Agents keep working with a\n    ``backend: fallback-*`` marker in the result.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::locate_binary","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::validate_object_id","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::validate_query","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::validate_platform","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_sync","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_search","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_show","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_matrix","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_note","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_notes","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::do_chain","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::run_action","modules/ttpscope_bridge.py::main"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
